ffense":[{"season":2024,"team":"DEN","distance":1.01,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Sean Payton"},{"season":2022,"team":"GB","distance":1.023,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Matt LaFleur"},{"season":2025,"team":"DEN","distance":1.151,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Sean Payton"},{"season":2022,"team":"LA","distance":1.217,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Sean McVay"},{"season":2022,"team":"JAX","distance":1.226,"shared":12,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"HOU","distance":0.2319,"shared":4,"play_caller":"DeMeco Ryans"},{"season":2022,"team":"NE","distance":0.2792,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"CAR","distance":0.3285,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Ejiro Evero"},{"season":2023,"team":"TEN","distance":0.3696,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"CHI","distance":0.3891,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Chiefs are 5-0 through week 6 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 140 to 83. Both sides of the ball have been strong, with the offense 5th in EPA per play and the defense 3rd in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the highest screen rate and the lowest eight man box rate in the league.","offense":"The Chiefs have one of the most efficient offenses in the league so far, ranking in the top eight in all five main efficiency measures. They have thrown more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score has not called for it. Schematically, they stand out for the highest screen rate and the highest play-action rate in the league. Patrick Mahomes has run the passing game, with Xavier Worthy leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Chiefs have one of the best defenses in the league this season, ranking 7th or better in all five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area has been EPA allowed per play, where it ranks 3rd, and its weakest has been sack rate, where it ranks 27th. Schematically, they have the lowest eight man box rate in the league.","special":"The Chiefs have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 77% of field goals, which is a little below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the quarterback, about 23% of the money on the books. Their secondary was among the youngest in the league.","players":"Patrick Mahomes has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,309 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Xavier Worthy and Travis Kelce leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. Kenneth Walker III has handled most of the work in the backfield with 85% of the carries. On defense, Nohl Williams leads the team with 1 sacks.","coaching":"Andy Reid is calling the offense as head coach and Steve Spagnuolo is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2024 Broncos under Sean Payton and the 2022 Packers under Matt LaFleur. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Texans under DeMeco Ryans and the 2022 Patriots.","trends":"The offense went from 11th in EPA per play in 2025 to 5th so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 12th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 3rd so far this season, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was play-action rate, which went from 15% to 35%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}